# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# The app has no client-side router, so this only matters for a deep link or a
# refresh on a path that was never a real file. 200 rather than 302 so the URL
# the learner sees is the one they asked for.
#
# Assets are matched before this rule, so a genuinely missing asset still 404s
# rather than being answered with the HTML shell — which is what turns a bad
# deploy into a silent white page.
/*    /index.html   200
